schema). (9) a config key: YES, edit! on :config, with register! for a new key. (10) a bin/ script: YES, :script. (11) a test fixture (test/seon/*.edn): NO, :path: tests. (12) deps.edn and pins: NO, :path: deps. RULE for all (decisions 2026-11-16, rails never guards, replacing the refusal): an edit of a path in the program's tree writes onto the branch like any other entry, never a silent disk write; so :path in the tree becomes the place of that path's file kind. GATE to switch everyone: data's seon_done pilot merged, and every kind above served on the branch, each proved by a driver (a Sonnet seon-driver with only seon_* tools) doing that edit and merging it. Drivers' findings are filed to these owners as they come. Proof: seon.repl-test/an-edit-of-every-kind-reaches-main-through-the-merge (one branch: each kind edited, merged, and present in main's files by the write-back; a :path in the tree held on the branch).\n\nSTATE 2026-11-16 (context, read at root [M result/aead7ab7]): unchanged since 11-15: seon.repl/place's methods are still :config :path :ns :doc :var :script, my.task/update! still writes main only, my.schema/register! writes the branch. Served: kinds 1, 3, 6 (an existing section), 9, 10; not served: 2 by edit!, 4, 5, 6 (a new page or section), 7, 8 by file, 11, 12, and :path still writes disk silently (the place every unserved kind falls to, so making :path in the tree a branch write serves kinds 8 by file, 11 and 12 at once). Drivers' findings filed so far (round 4's drivers, 2026-11-15): my.agent (prove's answer has no summary; a guessed my.agent/merge-main!) and seon.server (an eval after seon_done refused 'works no task now'). FEEDS tests' checklist step 7 (seon.proofs/a-test-forks-from-the-standing-system-and-a-binary-test-reruns-only-for-its-binary: every land through :prove and seon_done): a session can land through seon_done only the kinds served; what a Claude session's branch holds today beyond them (task files, schema files, fixtures, deps and pins, new wiki pages, deletions) has no inside path, so step 7 needs kinds 4, 7, 8 and 11 first (a session's usual land: code, a deletion, its task entry, a schema key, a fixture), then 2, 5, 6 and 12. ORDER of the drivers' proof: one driver per served kind edits and merges through seon_done on the standing system once tests' :prove carries a session's prove (step 6); each kind's driver run is its row here, with its turns.\n\nHOW A SESSION WORKS INSIDE, from context's audit of its own day (owner, 2026-11-16: use what exists, improve it for Seon agents first, never a duplicate). Each outside act and the existing inside mechanism it should have been: editing task files by script -> a task entry through the branch (kind 7; seon.system/changed-tx takes the file's text); checking an edited task file with a separate EDN read -> the checked write's speculate (pdb/speculate-db), which validates against the schema; classifying tests by regex over test files (131 counted) -> the program index, (seon.program/tests-reaching g 'seon.agent-test/with-agent) (112 in agent_test, 42 in repl_test, 194 tests reach in-agent) [result/ce130f97]; reading result files under target/results -> the results in the store (:seon.test/* facts, seon.proofs); running bin/test for one proof -> seon_prove with checkout and tree (the one test service); a hand-timed ticks comparison inside a test -> seon.cost/measure or seon.cost/proof and the test's :seon.test/estimate; shell loops waiting for a land slot -> none inside yet: the land queue (THE FOCUS piece 6) is that mechanism, and the loop is a stopgap named, never built on. What a driver or session lacks for each is this task's to file against the shared op. ORDER NOW (2026-11-16): first seon.repl/an-edit-of-an-in-tree-path-is-held-on-the-branch (kinds 8 and 11 and any in-tree file by path, replacing the :in-the-tree refusal: rails, never guards). AGREED with tests (design round, 2026-11-16): piece 6 drops the checkout-tree prove for sessions onc