  :seon.task/plan "Root's cold read after 9fb813b20e: 11.1 GB / 2.4B ticks [result/de815dbd], against an estimate of ~0.15 GB. The gap: each advance of the page walk between root's turns costs ~1 GB, 950 MB / 242M ticks of it in seon.ctx/moved, a d/datoms-diff of two branch values over eavt, for 33.7k net datoms (~28 KB a datom); patch 56 MB, walk 33 MB, a cold draw 118 MB [result/b9b95a01, dbbf1a3e]. What changed is a commit's datoms, always known (AGENTS.md section 4).\n\nPRIOR WORK: seon.merge/changed-datoms (merge.clj:591) reads the commits between two values (d/changes, netted by [e a v]: datahike/versioning.cljc:838) and diffs only uncommitted values. seon.merge requires no seon.ctx, so there's no cycle. Root agreed 2026-11-15 21:45.\n\nChange: moved's else branch is (merge/changed-datoms a b), gone then added, and the second diff path is deleted. Proof, red first, on the real path: a committed branch with a merge of main between two points (as root's is), with moved's cost O(d) at two sizes of untouched data. An in-memory diff may share structure, so a value-only fixture can pass before the fix.\n\nCOST: the commits' change sets, ~33.7k datoms x ~200 B = ~7 MB against 950 MB; root's cold read est ~0.2 GB after.\n\nThe seon.error/* stats churn (3.9k count/last-ms/first-ms rewritten a turn) is flow's, routed by root.\n\nMeasure today's and the fix's cost at root's REPL: root's branch db (seon.db/head conn (seon.db/on-main (seon.db/conn-main conn) branch)), the bases of root's model calls 1 and 2 (:seon.model-call/basis, select :commit :t), each read with seon.ctx.wire/db-at; then seon.cost/measure of (seon.ctx/moved d0 d1 nil), of seon.ctx/patch and of seon.render/walk with :moved, as result/b9b95a01 did. Run a long measure through bin/mcp call --port 7888 eval agent=root code=- in the background, not a foreground MCP call.\n\nFOUND (context, 2026-11-16 07:30) [M]: the change as written does not reach root's case. Between root's model calls 9 and 10 (bases 363eeaf6, 3e35f96c on :task-request-root, both :merge? true), d/changes refused :datahike/changes-unrecorded after 59M ticks [result/b8fd550d]: 3e35f96c's kept :base is main's commit (1d6f6da5, tx 536907093, then main's chain back 3000+ commits without 363eeaf6) [result/d9a27a49, b5121a55]. Cause, both ends read: seon.writer/merge-main-into (writer.clj:213) builds the merge as (d/with main tx) then force-branch! onto b, so the commit's value is built on main, and Datahike's changes walks :base (versioning.cljc:838), the commit a value was built on; a branch that merges main between two points has no :base path between them. So moved through changed-datoms falls back to the same datoms-diff, after a walk to the log's end. The fix is not here: landing 6 (seon.merge/a-merge-replays-the-sources-net-change, deps and data) applies main's net change onto the branch as new transactions, so the merge commit is built on the branch head and its :base is the branch's; then moved's else branch is changed-datoms and costs the commits between (main's change since the last merge-in plus the branch's own). Second finding, for deps (changed-datoms' edge): a from that is not on to's :base chain costs a walk to the log's end before the refusal (59M ticks here); a bound by from's t (stop at a commit older than from) ends it at once. NEXT: after landing 6, re-measure between two of root's merged bases, then the change and its proof."
